  "title": "How do I learn to identify birds? What equipment do I need to start b...",
  "description": "How do I learn to identify birds? What equipment do I need to start birding? The New York Times reporter and birding enthusiast Dodai Stewart takes a walk through Central Park in New York City and shares her tips for beginner birders.  Join us through September with the Cornell Lab of Ornithology to gather observations about the birds in your area. This data will help scientists understand better how birds are affected by forces like climate change and habitat loss. You can participate by signing up at the link in our bio.  Video by Gabriel Blanco, Karen Hanley, Rebecca Suner. #birdwatching #birding ",
